# Absent means absent: OS-dependent functions and upstream stubs are not in c.dll at P-1b. Called through the program's own prototypes (malloc, exit, printf, rand, localtime, fetestexcept, strsignal, and the stubs swprintf and strptime) the link fails, each name with N6's class line naming c.dll; called through the sysroot's headers they are undeclared, a compile error, in C (strsignal through <string.h> too) and in C++ (malloc through <stdlib.h>), and <fenv.h> is not installed. Objects the sysroot's headers declare but c.dll does not define (stdin, stdout, stderr, daylight, timezone, tzname, program_invocation_name and program_invocation_short_name) compile and fail at link, each name with no class line yet; so does assert with NDEBUG unset, whose __assert_fail fails at link with N6's class line. The C23 macros iscanonical and issignaling of <math.h> name functions c.dll does not ship, so a use is an undeclared-identifier error; l64a is undeclared in C17 and C23 and, through the program's own prototype, an undefined symbol (as are iscanonical and issignaling); <math.h> has none of the C99 comparison macros (isless, isunordered, ...), so a use is an undeclared-function error.
# Plan 5.19.1 rule 2 (absent until real: the generated headers declare only
# shipped entry points, so a use through <stdio.h> or <stdlib.h> is an
# undeclared-function error in C99, and a use through the program's own
# prototype is an undefined-symbol link error with N6's class line naming
# c.dll; no stub stands in), 5.19.4 (malloc and the heap, exit, stdio
# streams, rand and the localtime family wait for P-2 or P-3; swprintf and
# strptime are upstream stubs that only fail, so they stay absent),
# 5.19.15 (the two cases), 5.19.16 (fenv and the signal functions are
# undeclared: no fenv.h is installed and string.h has no strsignal), brief
# Q20 (a) and Q21 (a), 5.18.6 PL3 and 5.14.2 (N6: '>>> a C
# library function that the C library c.dll (msil64-unknown-dotnet) does not
# provide' when an input named c.dll takes part: here -lc from the sysroot,
# the driver's default library). The order of the undefined symbols is the
# linker's, so NAMES finds each one and SEQ checks that every error has the
# N6 line and a reference line after it. The programs never run. Section
# 12's row 'Contract 5.19.1 rule 2, 5.19.4 and the P-1b Goal amended
# (declared-but-absent names and memset_explicit, as built)' pins cases (3)
# and (5) here.
# Section 12's row 'Contract 5.19.4 and the P-1b Goal amended (exported but
# undeclared, as built)' pins cases (7) and (8): iscanonical, issignaling
# (with their f and l forms) and l64a are no entry points, because no
# installed header declares them. P-1b records the missing C99 comparison
# macros of llvm-libc's <math.h> (case (9)) as an upstream gap; the failure
# is a compile error, so it is loud. A link that writes --lto-emit-asm text
# cannot import c.dll (msil_link_output=il), so the test needs linked images.
# UNSUPPORTED: msil-link-output=il
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
#
# (1) The program's own prototypes: a link error per name, with N6.
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %t/own.c
